        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Columbia University, University of Colorado system\n- Places: Upper Manhattan, New York City, Colorado, Denver, Aurora\n- People: Robert Cunningham Humphreys\n- Topics: university types, campuses\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754.\n- Columbia University is officially named Columbia University in the City of New York.\n- Columbia University is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Columbia University is often cited as one of the world's most prestigious universities.\n- From 1926 to 1927, Robert Cunningham Humphreys was a student at Columbia University.\n- The University of Colorado system is a system of public universities in Colorado.\n- The University of Colorado system consists of four campuses: the University of Colorado Boulder, the University of Colorado Colorado Springs, the University of Colorado Denver in downtown Denver, and the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora.",
